stateDiagram-v2
    %% CURRENT implementation; derived Source proof timestamps, not a flow status column.
    [*] --> Absent
    Absent --> Issued: SignUpOtpChallengeRecorder.call / original bound candidate
    Issued --> Issued: same-flow resend / replace only unverified context
    Issued --> Verified: SignOtpCeremony.verify! / Source OTP consumption and proof commit
    Verified --> Verified: exact retry / same binding and fixed live result deadline
    Issued --> Unavailable: OTP deadline or parent terminal / refusal predicate
    Verified --> Unavailable: result deadline, release or lost live authority / refusal predicate
    note right of Issued
        APP/COM email and telephone store the original flow and nonce digest.
        Owner, candidate, destination, counter and keyed code digest bind the challenge.
        Owning Ticket, Source owner and Contact locks precede decisions.
        Both candidate and shared destination failure limits remain authoritative.
        Enqueue follows Ticket binding; transport checks the original counter under locks.
    end note
    note right of Verified
        Source transaction consumes OTP and establishes immutable verified_at.
        Subsequent four Ticket progression writes share one Ticket transaction.
        Result expiry is min(verification plus 60 seconds, original Ticket deadline).
        Retry compares the same input and respects shared/candidate failure limits.
        No proof reissue, TTL extension, binding finalization or root issuance occurs here.
        HTTP phase progression and its replay rules remain separate.
    end note
